cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Annotated Corpus of Ancient Testamentary Literature
message: >-
  If you use this corpus, please cite it using the metadata from this file.
type: dataset
abstract: >-
  Manual genre annotation of 33 ancient testamentary texts (Greek, Latin) in 38
  text versions, comprising 3,451 annotation instances over a repertoire of 32
  feature codes on four levels. The annotations record features typical of the
  genre — narrative framing, speaker, addressees, proximity of death, ethical
  exhortation, eschatological perspective and others. Annotated with CATMA;
  published as TEI standoff annotations. For 17 of the 38 text versions the base
  text cannot be redistributed; for these the annotations are published with
  character offsets, SHA-256 checksums and a reconstruction script.
